<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch unadjusted unemployment falls in Feb-April.</title>
<headline>Dutch unadjusted unemployment falls in Feb-April.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch non-seasonally adjusted unemployment fell to an average of 399,000 in February-April from 415,000 in January-March, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT NON-SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			   Feb-April 97   Jan-March 97   Feb-April 96</p>
<p> total number	   399,000	  415,000	  465,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force    6.0		6.2		7.0</p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			   Feb-April 97   Jan-March 97   Feb-April 96</p>
<p> total number	   387,000	  398,000	  453,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force    5.8		6.0		6.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Economists polled by Reuters had expected an unadjusted February-April unemployment figure of 404,000 and a seasonally adjusted figure of 393,000.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
